    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0224" n="142" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg142"/>

                <head>Mr. Marsh to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 117.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Turin,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received from the minister of
                    foreign affairs official notice that the office of that ministry will be
                    transferred to Florence on the fifteenth day of <pb facs="0225" n="143"
                        xml:id="pg143"/> May next, but I have been since informed by the secretary
                    general that it is doubtful whether the minister of foreign affairs Will be at
                    that city in person before the end of the month.</p>
                <p>It is understood that the King leaves Turin for Florence to-day, but no formal
                    announcement of his change of residence has been made.</p>
                <p>I shall remain at Turin until the removal of the public offices actually takes
                    place, and shall then proceed to the new capital.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEORGE P. MARSH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
